# App Status Check and Rebuild Guide

This guide helps you check what parts of the WhoCares app are running and how to properly rebuild after code changes.

## Quick Status Checks

### Check All Running Services
```bash
# Check if API is running (port 3000)
lsof -i :3000 | grep LISTEN

# Check if Metro bundler is running (port 8081)
lsof -i :8081 | grep LISTEN

# Check if PostgreSQL is running
docker ps | grep postgres

# Check running simulators
xcrun simctl list devices | grep "Booted"
```

### Check Individual Services

#### API Server Status
```bash
# Test if API is responding
curl http://localhost:3000/api

# Find what's using port 3000
lsof -i :3000
```

#### Metro Bundler Status
```bash
# Check Metro process
ps aux | grep "react-native start" | grep -v grep

# Check if Metro is responding
curl http://localhost:8081/status
```

## Rebuilding After Code Changes

### Quick Rebuild (Most Cases)
For most code changes, just reload the app:
1. Press `r` in the Metro terminal
2. Or shake device/press Cmd+R in simulator

### Medium Rebuild (When Quick Doesn't Work)
```bash
# From project root
cd apps/mobile && npx react-native clean
cd ../.. && npx nx run-ios mobile -- --scheme="Mobile"
```

### Full Clean Rebuild (After Pulling New Code)
When you pull fresh commits or the app shows old cached builds:

```bash
# 1. Stop all services
pkill -f "react-native start" || echo "Metro not running"
pkill -f "nx serve api" || echo "API not running"

# 2. Clean everything
cd apps/mobile && npx react-native clean
rm -rf ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/*
cd ios && rm -rf build
watchman watch-del-all && watchman shutdown-server

# 3. Reinstall iOS dependencies
pod deintegrate && pod install

# 4. Return to project root
cd ../../..

# 5. Start services fresh
npx nx start mobile --reset-cache  # In one terminal
npx nx serve api                    # In another terminal (or use PORT=3001 if 3000 is taken)

# 6. Build and run
npx nx run-ios mobile -- --scheme="Mobile" --simulator="iPhone 16 Pro"
```

## Service Management

### Starting Services

#### Database
```bash
docker compose up -d
```

#### API Server
```bash
npx nx serve api

# If port 3000 is in use:
PORT=3001 npx nx serve api
```

#### Metro Bundler
```bash
npx nx start mobile

# With cache reset:
npx nx start mobile --reset-cache
```

#### iOS App
```bash
# Basic
npx nx run-ios mobile

# With correct scheme (often needed)
npx nx run-ios mobile -- --scheme="Mobile"

# Target specific simulator
npx nx run-ios mobile -- --scheme="Mobile" --simulator="iPhone 16 Pro"
```

### Stopping Services

```bash
# Stop Metro bundler
pkill -f "react-native start"

# Stop API server
pkill -f "nx serve api"

# Stop database
docker compose down

# Kill process on specific port
kill -9 $(lsof -ti:3000)  # Kill whatever is on port 3000
kill -9 $(lsof -ti:8081)  # Kill whatever is on port 8081
```

## Common Issues and Quick Fixes

### "Old build showing in simulator"
```bash
# Clean and rebuild
cd apps/mobile && npx react-native clean
rm -rf ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/*
cd ../.. && npx nx run-ios mobile -- --scheme="Mobile"
```

### "Port already in use"
```bash
# Find what's using the port
lsof -i :3000

# Kill it
kill -9 $(lsof -ti:3000)

# Or run on different port
PORT=3001 npx nx serve api
```

### "Watchman crawl warnings"
```bash
watchman watch-del '/Users/rheeger/Code/rheeger/who-cares'
watchman watch-project '/Users/rheeger/Code/rheeger/who-cares'
```

### "Scheme 'mobile' not found"
Always use capital M:
```bash
npx nx run-ios mobile -- --scheme="Mobile"
```

### "Node version mismatch in Xcode"
Update [.xcode.env.local](mdc:apps/mobile/ios/.xcode.env.local):
```bash
export NODE_BINARY=$(which node)
```

## Quick Reference Commands

### Check Everything
```bash
# One command to check all services
echo "=== API (3000) ===" && lsof -i :3000 | grep LISTEN && \
echo "=== Metro (8081) ===" && lsof -i :8081 | grep LISTEN && \
echo "=== Database ===" && docker ps | grep postgres && \
echo "=== Simulators ===" && xcrun simctl list devices | grep "Booted"
```

### Nuclear Clean (Reset Everything)
```bash
# Run from project root
cd apps/mobile && npx react-native clean && \
rm -rf ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/* && \
cd ios && rm -rf build && pod deintegrate && pod install && \
cd ../../.. && \
watchman watch-del-all && watchman shutdown-server
```

### Standard Development Startup
```bash
# Terminal 1: Database
docker compose up -d

# Terminal 2: API
npx nx serve api

# Terminal 3: Metro
npx nx start mobile

# Terminal 4: Build and run
npx nx run-ios mobile -- --scheme="Mobile"
```

## Pro Tips

1. **After pulling new code**: Always do at least a Medium Rebuild
2. **Metro not updating**: Kill it and restart with `--reset-cache`
3. **Multiple simulators**: Close extras in Simulator app to avoid confusion
4. **API changes**: The API hot-reloads, but you may need to restart if adding new dependencies
5. **Use the Metro menu**: Press `i` in Metro terminal instead of running build commands

